<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing wavenumber at 666 nm in the Astyanax cave morph — Code-to-model traceability: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "dispersion_eigenvalue, the pseudo-spectral step, and the Lean theorems (trace, determinant, drive, discriminant, equal-diffusivity failure, wavenumber bracket, 36-37x sibling ratio) point at the same integer Jacobian. The composite helper still contains an unused resampled buffer." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing wavenumber at 666 nm in the Astyanax cave morph — Model fidelity to source: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script integrates Schnakenberg kinetics with a Fourier pseudo-spectral step and compares growth rates to the eigenvalue of gamma*J - k^2 D. Parameters are chosen so the fastest mode sits on the card wavelength; they are not fitted to a cavefish time series. Eye and neuromast pathways are excluded from the state vector, which matches the claim boundary." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing wavenumber at 666 nm in the Astyanax cave morph — Morphometric validation: 76/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Eleven Fourier modes give Pearson r = 0.99997 and RMSE = 0.00455 against the analytical growth rate. The nonlinear radial peak is 660.7 nm against the 665.6 nm linear calibration (about 0.7 percent low). sigma(0) = -0.1. The voucher melanin-dark fraction is 0.002, against an Oca2-null reference of 0. No KS test and no ablation metric are in the pass-1 table." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-growth-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-growth-rmse>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-homogeneous-mode-growth>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-melanin-dark-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-stripe-wavelength-nm>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing wavenumber at 666 nm in the Astyanax cave morph — MorphoEval overall 77.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1. Schnakenberg reaction-diffusion on a periodic 72 by 112 patch, with Du:Dv = 2:20 and gamma = 1, calibrated so the fastest linear mode has wavelength 6.656e-7 m (666 nm nominal, Holocene cave morph, 0 Ma). Forward-Euler integration of the linear Fourier-mode ODE matches the closed-form growth rate at Pearson r = 0.99997 (RMSE 0.00455, 11 modes). The nonlinear patch selects 660.7 nm. The cave-morph voucher (CC BY-SA 4.0, Seb Morič) is masked and used as a visualization carrier; the photograph cannot resolve 666 nm. sigma(k=0) = -0.1, so the homogeneous state is stable. No diffusion-ratio sweep, no Du = Dv ablation in the reported metrics, and no flank KS comparison yet. Overall 77.4/100 (faithfulness 74.4, reproducibility 84.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 82, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 58, Morphometric validation 76, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/astyanax_mexicanus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 380391 B, 1512×528 px, artifact_sha256 6b4715eaa25378a971dc38aebd2b796c9ce50ab36f3b15b51e08ae4933d6c5b3 (sha256 6b4715eaa25378a971dc38aebd2b796c9ce50ab36f3b15b51e08ae4933d6c5b3), spec_fingerprint 567daaa26ea32b6e0db869c7c7df6b1cf14d5ac54c7e7b02f34d577ba1dab69a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 567daaa26ea32b6e0db869c7c7df6b1cf14d5ac54c7e7b02f34d577ba1dab69a; artifact_sha256: 6b4715eaa25378a971dc38aebd2b796c9ce50ab36f3b15b51e08ae4933d6c5b3; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/astyanax_mexicanus_turing_wavelength_s0/astyanax_mexicanus_specimen.jpg=b7b2d7744b19592f..., datasets/astyanax_mexicanus_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=a4f57d067c37118a...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) derived diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) gave the two-species kinetics. Murray (1981) applied the wavelength idea to animal coat markings. | Cavefish pigment loss is genetic: oca2 albinism (Protas et al. 2006) and mc1r depigmentation (Gross et al. 2009). Pigment-cell regression is a late melanogenesis step (McCauley, Hixon and Jeffery 2004). | Eye degeneration is Hedgehog-dependent lens apoptosis (Yamamoto, Stock and Jeffery 2004). Neuromast expansion is a lateral-line phenotype tied to feeding behavior (Yoshizawa et al. 2010). Jeffery (2009) reviews both.; reconstructed_in_script: The 6.656e-7 m wavelength is the loop-card scale, not a length reported by those papers. The script places the fastest linear mode on that length by the metres-per-pixel calibration. | Pass-1 numbers: dispersion Pearson r = 0.99997, RMSE = 0.00455, nonlinear wavelength 660.7 nm, body melanin-dark fraction 0.002 on the voucher, scale ratio 36.33 against the 24 µm sibling.; transfer_boundary: The composite GIF paints the subcellular patch onto a whole-body photograph. That is a visualization, not evidence that the voucher resolves 666 nm, and it does not transfer to surface-fish stripe spacing.; does_not_claim: Does not claim that optic-cup degeneration or neuromast expansion are outputs of k_c. | Does not claim a cavefish morphogen pair has been identified. Schnakenberg kinetics are a minimal carrier. | Does not claim the chronoseries has a fossil predecessor. The series is the single Holocene cave morph at 0 Ma.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Sweep the diffusion ratio Dv/Du and show that the selected wavelength moves monotonically. Pass 1 renders a single (Du, Dv, gamma).'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Add the Du = Dv ablation and report that the maximum growth rate is negative, matching the Lean equal-diffusivity theorem.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Segment the voucher flank and compare its orientation histogram to the simulated patch with a KS statistic. The pass-1 melanin fraction is a threshold count, not a distributional test.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Drop the unused resampled buffer in compose_frame and keep the signed-field composite as the only render path.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 7.74e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing wavenumber at 666 nm in the Astyanax cave morph — Parameter expressivity: 58/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Du, Dv, gamma and beta are single values. The fastest-mode calibration shows that the spatial unit controls the reported wavelength, but pass 1 does not sweep the diffusion ratio or show that lambda moves monotonically. Expressivity is stated, not exercised." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 5.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

