<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Turing wavenumber at 666 nm in the Astyanax cave morph (Astyanax mexicanus (Holocene cave morph, 0 Ma))",
        "Turing wavenumber at 666 nm in the Astyanax cave morph faithfully reproduces Astyanax mexicanus (Holocene cave morph, 0 Ma) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Astyanax mexicanus (Holocene cave morph, 0 Ma) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Astyanax mexicanus (Holocene cave morph, 0 Ma)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a cavefish morphogen pair has been identified. Schnakenberg kinetics are a minimal carrier.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim that optic-cup degeneration or neuromast expansion are outputs of k_c.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the chronoseries has a fossil predecessor. The series is the single Holocene cave morph at 0 Ma.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass-1 numbers: dispersion Pearson r = 0.99997, RMSE = 0.00455, nonlinear wavelength 660.7 nm, body melanin-dark fraction 0.002 on the voucher, scale ratio 36.33 against the 24 µm sibling.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The 6.656e-7 m wavelength is the loop-card scale, not a length reported by those papers. The script places the fastest linear mode on that length by the metres-per-pixel calibration.",
        "reported_in_source: Cavefish pigment loss is genetic: oca2 albinism (Protas et al. 2006) and mc1r depigmentation (Gross et al. 2009). Pigment-cell regression is a late melanogenesis step (McCauley, Hixon and Jeffery 2004).",
        "reported_in_source: Eye degeneration is Hedgehog-dependent lens apoptosis (Yamamoto, Stock and Jeffery 2004). Neuromast expansion is a lateral-line phenotype tied to feeding behavior (Yoshizawa et al. 2010). Jeffery (2009) reviews both.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) derived diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) gave the two-species kinetics. Murray (1981) applied the wavelength idea to animal coat markings.",
        "transfer_boundary: The composite GIF paints the subcellular patch onto a whole-body photograph. That is a visualization, not evidence that the voucher resolves 666 nm, and it does not transfer to surface-fish stripe spacing." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Astyanax mexicanus (Holocene Cave Morph (Extant))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Pisces (Ichthyes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Astyanax" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/astyanax_mexicanus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Astyanax mexicanus (Holocene cave morph, 0 Ma); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) derived diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) gave the two-species kinetics. Murray (1981) applied the wavelength idea to animal coat markings. | Cavefish pigment loss is genetic: oca2 albinism (Protas et al. 2006) and mc1r depigmentation (Gross et al. 2009). Pigment-cell regression is a late melanogenesis step (McCauley, Hixon and Jeffery 2004). | Eye degeneration is Hedgehog-dependent lens apoptosis (Yamamoto, Stock and Jeffery 2004). Neuromast expansion is a lateral-line phenotype tied to feeding behavior (Yoshizawa et al. 2010). Jeffery (2009) reviews both.; reconstructed_in_script: The 6.656e-7 m wavelength is the loop-card scale, not a length reported by those papers. The script places the fastest linear mode on that length by the metres-per-pixel calibration. | Pass-1 numbers: dispersion Pearson r = 0.99997, RMSE = 0.00455, nonlinear wavelength 660.7 nm, body melanin-dark fraction 0.002 on the voucher, scale ratio 36.33 against the 24 µm sibling.; transfer_boundary: The composite GIF paints the subcellular patch onto a whole-body photograph. That is a visualization, not evidence that the voucher resolves 666 nm, and it does not transfer to surface-fish stripe spacing.; does_not_claim: Does not claim that optic-cup degeneration or neuromast expansion are outputs of k_c. | Does not claim a cavefish morphogen pair has been identified. Schnakenberg kinetics are a minimal carrier. | Does not claim the chronoseries has a fossil predecessor. The series is the single Holocene cave morph at 0 Ma.]; phenomenon_size: 484 nm (4.836e-07 m, log10=-6.316 m, tier=2_macromolecular_100nm); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 484 nm to 1.1 mm): 484 nm:astyanax-mexicanus-bioelectric-polarity, 1.5 µm:astyanax-mexicanus-vertex-packing, 24 µm:astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength, 48 µm:astyanax-mexicanus-clock-wavefront, 109 µm:astyanax-mexicanus-morphogen-condensation, 133 µm:astyanax-mexicanus-elastic-buckling, 151 µm:astyanax-mexicanus-flux-canalization, 212 µm:astyanax-mexicanus-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.07.017>,
